@qodo-ai-reviewer Added runtime sanitization for persisted plugin state in both `server.ts` and `tui.ts`, so malformed JSON now safely falls back to sane defaults instead of being trusted blindly. `disabled` is filtered to string arrays, `levels` is filtered to valid `lite|full|ultra` values, and the server now falls back safely before `RULES[...]` lookup so we never push an undefined rule.

I also sanity-tested the plugin/package loading path against opencode’s plugin loader tests after the change.

