The current `.opencode-plugin` folder is a valid opencode plugin package because it exposes `./server` and `./tui` in `package.json`, so the runtime can load both entrypoints from the plugin array. To make that clearer and more idiomatic, I updated the README in 79fb558 to recommend adding the plugin directory itself to `opencode.json`:
```json
{
  "plugin": ["/path/to/caveman/plugins/caveman/.opencode-plugin"]
}
instead of wiring separate server.ts / tui.ts file paths manually.

